Early-Z split (0170/0179) for interpolated presentation: the split decision and its two
pipelines are cached with the draw cache (two whole-config pipeline lookups per draw before), and
with GX_AURORA_ACCURACY_EARLY_Z_MERGE consecutive draws with the same state are merged into one
split pair (depth half and colour half extended alike). A foyer frame had ~16,000 split draws,
all unmerged: replaying it took ~25 ms on the FIFO thread (presentation at ~35 fps at a 120
target); cached ~11 ms, merged ~4 ms. AURORA_EARLY_Z_MERGE=0/1/ab overrides the flag.

